{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/77284-force-relationship","id":77284,"title":"Force Relationship","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-22T13:09:52-08:00","id":77284,"title":"Force Relationship","content":"So, it kinda feels like some sorta resistance roll ought to be available for this Exploit, particularly for supernatural targets. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:56:01-08:00","id":77337,"title":"","content":"I agree with you.<br /> <br /> While there is no &quot;resisting exploits&quot; entry like there is for &quot;resisting embeds&quot; (p 124) I feel that the table could apply to exploits without any serious detrimental effects.<br /> <br /> If one of my players attempted to use this power on an a named NPC of some import I'd probably rule that the target can roll their resolve + supernatural resistance start to contest the action. If the target had a shield that interacted with the supernatural - like mind OR fate shield (or similar thing) then I would be okay with using the Clash of wills rule (p. 122).<br /> <br /> If there was a dispute I'd be very willing to give a player a beat over it and encourage them to move on (I'd go as high as one experience but then I'd be grumpy).<br /> <br /> In the end how important is it to the story? if it's not really important I'd let it go, but if it had the potential to radically alter the game, I'd probably talk th